 rcbi41@muvms3.bitnet (Stan Perrine = Mr. Computer) writes:

> OK, maybe I'm missing something really simple, but
> I'm only on the 2nd level of the dungeon, and I
> can't find anyway to get down. My Elf obviously
> hasn't obtained any type of teleportation
> device/control and there are no stairs to be
> found. I read on this group once that some levels
> of the dungeon have no stairs...but what's the
> point of doing this on the 2nd level. There isn't
> a whole lot I can do being only a 4th level Elf.
> Should I just start over or what?

Well, there's _always_ a way down from level two to
level three.  If you don't see the stairs down,
there are several possibilities:

1) It is under something else. Go stand on every
artifact on the level, and see if you find some
stairs too.

2) There is a hidden door you haven't found. An elf
has automatic searching, so as a first pass, just
run around the perimeter of every room a half dozen
times. Some doors are _incredibly hard to find, like
requiring 100 searches or more standing right next
to them; you're likely to starve first, so save such
searching for last ditch, and concentrate on walls
facing likely open spaces to contain the missing
room (though the occasional passage will wrap
completely around a room to get to another room, so
this isn't failsafe).

3) There is a hidden passage you haven't found. This
one is really nasty. The best thing to do is to look
at the layout, and realize that every passage
_starts_ as a fairly direct route from one room to
another. Are there passages that don't seem aimed at
a room? Then there is a room in that direction, but
the passage you see might not be the one going
there; passages do die out when the dwarves get
drunk and forget where they were digging. ;-) Try
searching at the ends of blind passages, at corners
in passages that might really be "T" junctions
instead, at the bases of "U" shaped passages that
seem pointless.

4) There is a hidden door or passage behind a
boulder blocking a passage. Nastiest off all. Take
off and drop everything, sneak past the boulder, and
search for a continuation. If you find it, remember
that there are very likely _lots_ of random monsters
that have shown up on the other side during all this
searching. Push the boulder past your stuff, and get
dressed and ready to fight before pressing on.

5) Go back and search likely walls about 20 times
per space until you have your god so angry even
prayer won't prevent starvation.

6) Maintain a noble sense of humor.  Lost nethack
games are learning experiences, and you lose most
nethack games you play.

